Feature: Source owned action staging
 Scenario: Only issuable exact generations cross receiving
  Given canonical decimal generation text at the u64 maximum
  Then native and web admit the same exact token without rounding
  And overflow, signs, leading zeros and extra digits refuse before producer or edits
 Scenario: Private parsed request values move after bounded admission
  Given a closed original Pack request with strictly ordered UTF8 map keys
  When original funded receiving completes its census and exact typed movement
  Then payload ownership moves without a deep clone
  And duplicate or unordered incoming map keys refuse before publication
 Scenario: Stale source answers cannot overwrite local staging
  Given an original request generation and canonical source revision
  When a response or field event belongs to another generation or revision
  Then no staged argument changes and Execute remains unavailable
 Scenario: Exact nested command data remains ephemeral until Execute
  Given decimal identities and binary64 words beyond JavaScript safe integers
  When a field event changes one nested argument
  Then siblings and exact values remain unchanged
  And Execute sends exactly one descriptor containing the closed application
 Scenario: Typed choices retain provenance
  Given released declaration choices and actual referenced source enumeration values
  Then each choice carries its complete typed value and original provenance
  And neither source choices nor reference candidates are truncated suggestions
 Scenario: Every query is replaceable and cancellable
  When staging or source revision changes
  Then the original outstanding query is cancelled
  And only the current answer can become visible
